      ],
      "text": "This is an answer written by a candidate who achieved a Band 6.0 score.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        459.0346984863281,
        517.6812744140625,
        497.7525939941406
      ],
      "text": "If we look at the pictures we will see how Beechwood Farm has changed along\nthe time.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        510.8746643066406,
        515.89208984375,
        629.0336303710938
      ],
      "text": "Years ago, in 1950, Beachwood Farm was a tipycal farm. A track crossed the\nfarm, so farmers could reach the barn and the farmhouse passing by the fruit\ntrees, and the place where the soft fruits and the vegetables were growing. At\nthe opposite side of the truck, was the field where the sheeps were situated.\nThat was close to the farmhouse, were chickens were also situated. All the\nfarm was sourrounded, at the south, by a river.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        642.0347290039062,
        516.6553344726562,
        760.192626953125
      ],
      "text": "Nowadays, the farm has suffered changes. Modern life brought to the farm\nsome needs to survive. The main change was the road that replaced the track.\nNow is easyer to arrive any place in the farm. There is a parking zone near the\nroad where the sheeps used to eat grass. We can also find a camping field and\nSolar panels in that zone. Another parking zone can be find where the solar\npanels are situated. Just in front of the first parking zone we can see a farm\n"
    }
